  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a SwiftHFR reader on iOS 27, including iPhone Duo, I want the reader's page controls to be the legacy ones, shown as system glass bottom-bar items, and messages to scroll under the bars, so the reader matches legacy and the HIG and its controls move to the side on the Duo cover screen.\n\nPart of #545 (M4; the HIG wins and divergences are recorded in GAP). **This lot absorbs #428** (UXD-10, legacy page controls): it is the same code, so the PR closes both.\n\n### Scope\n- **Page bar** (`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:54-56, 266-300`, an `HStack` with `.background(.bar)` in `safeAreaInset`): becomes `ToolbarItemGroup(placement: .bottomBar)` with the legacy layout from `MessagesView.swift:4756-4800` @ `2440d79`, per #428:\n  - `.visibilityPriority(.high)` on page navigation and reply (iOS 27.0+, verified on the live docs);\n  - `ToolbarSpacer` (iOS 26.0+).\n  - The legacy \"…\" page menu uses another symbol or the system overflow menu. The Duo HIG reserves the ellipsis for overflow; record this in the spec as a divergence.\n- **Toolbar grouping:** the top bar has up to 5 items:\n  - `TopicReaderView.swift:62,67`;\n  - `Composer/ReaderReplyFlow.swift:30`;\n  - `Reader/Search/ReaderSearchFlow.swift:21`;\n  - `Offline/ReaderOfflineSave.swift:17`.\n  Group them (HIG Toolbars: at most three groups). Change the circled symbol at `:68` to a plain one.\n- **Web view under the bars:**\n  - the content extends under the top and bottom bars (`TopicReaderView.swift:38-43`: `ignoresSafeArea` + `WKWebView.obscuredContentInsets`, iOS 26.0+, or automatic insets);\n  - the scroll edge effect replaces opaque fills.\n- **Scroll restore:**\n  - `ReaderWebController.swift:111,242` (`contentOffset`) and the LOT-111 positions must account for the new insets, so a page never reopens shifted by the bar height;\n  - add tests on the model or the offset math wherever it can be tested.\n- **Reader toast** (`TopicReaderView.swift:159-164`): `.glassEffect(in: .capsule)`; remove the magic `.padding(.bottom, 56)`.\n- **Contrast:** the tinted message headers (`reader.css:58-59,113-121`) under the bars. Check them on the Mac; change the CSS only if needed.\n\n**Coordination:**\n- **#424 / PR #540** (hide the tab bar while reading) touches 6 lines of `TopicReaderView.swift`. It is not blocking. Rebase on `dev-swift` once #540 merges. The Mac check of this lot runs after #540 is merged.\n- **LOT-185** owns every file outside `Reader/`, except `ReaderReplyFlow.swift`, `ReaderSearchFlow.swift` and `ReaderOfflineSave.swift:17`, which are toolbar items owned here. `ReaderOfflineSave.swift:62` (the top strip) belongs to LOT-185.\n\n### Depends on\n#540 for the hand check only.\n\n### Model\nOpus 5.5 → Fable 5.1 review. The scroll offsets and `WKWebView` insets are the regression risk.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] #428's acceptance criteria are met.\n- [ ] No `.background(.bar)` remains in `Reader/`. The web view's content runs under the bars, and the toast offset is gone.\n- [ ] Scroll restore and LOT-111 positions reopen at the same message with the new insets (tests where testable; Mac check otherwise).\n- [ ] The divergences (the ellipsis, the grouping) are recorded in `docs/lots/LOT-186-reader-chrome.md`, with the HIG URL and the legacy file:line.\n- [ ] SwiftLint strict is green, and so is the CI `App build + tests` job.\n- [ ] The PR has a \"Mac check needed\" section: iPhone 18 Pro + iPad + Duo poses; light, dark, Dynamic Type XL, Reduce Transparency, Increase Contrast; dark brightness 0–150 %; reopening a topic at its saved position.",
